 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+- **Self-hosted WebSockets for change delivery.** Committed revisions are published to browsers over server-operated WebSocket sessions. Five-second HTTPS polling was rejected as slower and read-heavier; a hosted realtime service was rejected to avoid recurring fees and provider coupling. Self-hosting accepts connection-capacity and reconnect operations as the cost of fast updates without a vendor. See `docs/decisions/change-delivery-approach.md`.
